  "authorizationBoundary": "External Service CREATE accepts an optional closed TCP healthCheck subset through its existing typed plan owner. Exactly the five caller fields are reviewed; port is required 1..65535 and four omitted timing fields are not filled. The positive integer timing subset matches existing typed Service validation; native metadata declares no timing minimum or defaults. HTTP controls and unknown, null, wrong-type or fractional values are rejected. The detached native body alone carries requestLine=null. Native schema/role projection is rechecked before preparation and dispatch; exact TCP readback is required for a verified receipt. No UPDATE healthCheck support, new HTTP route, operation semantics, role/Key grant, or approval bypass. Omitted healthCheck retains None and ordinary Service health checks are unchanged.",
